Z||000000||mrgone||07-10-2001||02:45 PM||||i usually put plus octane in (mid grade) my 2m4 5speed and i reset the trip when i fill the tank. im in canada so i dont know the mpg i get but i know its very poor. i filled the tank last night (needle up to full), it took 12$ of plus (73c a litre had a 1/4 tank when i got to the pump) and drove 26 kms since then. in that 26 kms the needle has dropped 1/4 tank. this is city driving and i usually take the tach up to 4000+rpm off 1st gear but then shift lower after that.<P>i know those are crappy numbers to work with, but 1/4 tank in 26kms? thats not good. that would mean i get 100kms to a tank of gas. the only engine code i get is the IAC valve, ive replaced the map sensor, the connectors are clean... the car doesnt smoke.<BR>i run carb cleaner through it usually when i put gas in it. it doesnt idle high..<P>any suggestions? the gas guage seems to work fine because when the guage is low i can put the correct amount of gas in when i fill it.<BR>but i havent let the tank run dry to be sure.<P><BR>oh and i did do a basic tuneup 1500kms or so ago. changed oil and filter, plugs, air filter, pcv valve.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">    <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B><p>[This message has been edited by mrgone (edited 07-10-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000001||Leadfoot||07-10-2001||03:16 PM||||Are you sure your gauge is working properly?  I have just put in a rebuilt v6 and noticed my gas mileage is poor (this is after a complete tune-up).  However, I noticed that what the gauge shows does not represent the actual amount of fuel.  It is off a couple of gallons.  Check it out by filling up the tank, drive it till you have a half tank and pump it back up again and see if you are getting the right numbers.  The fieros hold about 10 gallons so half of that would be 5 gallons.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||07-10-2001||03:33 PM||||ignore the gas gauge till its down around a 1/4, then fill the car up and check your real milage from fillup to fillup.<P>  the gauge is nowheres near accurate at any position - once you have an idea of what your mpg performace is, use your trip odo to determine when its time to fill your tank back up.<P>  My V6 auto gets about 20mpg in the city, on the highway last week I was getting about 25.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||07-10-2001||05:57 PM||||Hey MRGONE!<BR>First, have you checked your tire pressure? I know that is a simple step, but it makes a BIG difference on mine!<BR>Secondly, does your car sort of surge at cruse? It could be a stuck EGR valve.<BR>If it is stuck, follow the shop manual on cleaning it. Once it is clean and seals with NO leak, reinstall it with a NEW gasket...<BR>The new gasket is important, if you use the old gasket, you could get an air leak and toast the engine in a few hundred miles...<BR>Lastly, check your TPS with an ohm meter...<BR>If it is bad, it will not have a smooth resistance change from one end to the other...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrgone||07-11-2001||02:00 AM||||yes the car does sort of surge....<BR>and i think my guage is accurate, as i said it took 12$ of gas<P>ill go fill my tires up right now<P><BR>please elaborate on this EGR valve thingy<BR>while i read my haynes manual<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">    <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B><p>[This message has been edited by mrgone (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrgone||07-11-2001||03:25 AM||||how many litres are in 5 gallons?||||reg||1
Z||000006||overlord||07-11-2001||08:59 AM||||5 gallons is about 20-21 litres roughly.<P>Yes check ur tire preasure!  It makes all the difference in gas mileage if even one tire is low.<P>In the winter when i had 1 tire with 0psi and another at 5psi (YES 0)...i was getting about 15 milespergallon.   Now summertime and tires normal im getting double.||||reg||1
Z||000007||deceler8||07-11-2001||11:17 AM||||Another thing to look at is your E-brake...if it's dragging, your mileage will be affected.<P>It's not uncommon for the cables to sieze and not fully release.||||reg||1
